6. LEARNING OUTCOMES
Students should become practitioners who:
• are familiar with pertinent issues in the field of education and be comfortable in the use of advanced data analysis tools
and techniques that assist in finding sustainable and innovative solutions using publications and other verifiable
outcomes, especially in their programme areas of teaching specialisation;
• possess verifiable skills in designing and implementing monitoring and evaluation tools that serve to improve their
practice, informed by foundational concepts and theories;
• exhibit quality teaching skills that inform their day-to-day practice and the ability to facilitate learning among their
learners;

